  "visualReview": {
    "coverage": "Viewed all 64 pages and 8 covers in eight 3×3 contact sheets, then re-inspected corrected sheets. Selected full-size views: 0241 p05 and p08; 0242 p06 and p08; 0243 p05, p07 and p08; 0244 p01, p07 and p08; 0245 p05, p06 and p08; 0246 p05 and p06; 0247 p07 and p08; 0248 p06 and p07.",
    "notes": [
      "0241: the grey mouse retains white whiskers and a brick-red vest; the small cloth goose has blue wings and a soft orange beak. A single red bean remains on the mesh during the separate trial, while the smaller millet falls into the bowl. The batch uses a visibly larger basin. The finished stuffed bed, returned red-bean jar, closed sewing box and rehung sieve form the ending; grain is not eaten.",
      "0242: the chest has four wooden feet and one round brass clasp. Its mouth is drawn only on the inside of a raised lid, and is absent when the lid is closed during quiet companionship. The otter has a single cream bag: carried while walking and set down during rest. The empty bench space, leaf, closed lid and final small opening preserve the sequence.",
      "0243: the square suitcase has two brass catches and no limbs. Pajamas remain absent from pages 1–6, then blue checks appear above the small pillow when the suitcase opens in the new room. The old room has one red mushroom outside its window, while the new room has three. The girl carries the case by its handle, and the sleeping child fits on the mattress in the final page.",
      "0244: the same pink wooden peach is hidden, found and passed into the next round. The sand tray distinguishes the shaded section from the sunny right edge; the fan rests on the tray after the misunderstanding. The sand child faces away for hiding, and the crab turns its back on the final page without closed eyes. Character bodies sit behind the tray edge, with searching hands visible above the sand.",
      "0245: the grey-white stone with two brown cheek spots stays on one cloth cushion at the windowsill. The failed strong breath produces broken-film marks and droplets; three small bubbles appear in the short-breath trial. The continuous gentle breath makes an attached film, followed by one detached bubble. The last page has a newly inflated film after dipping, without duplicating the previous bubble; reflections include the red roof and paper pinwheel.",
      "0246: the characters retain the blue vest and green apron with glasses. The large white daisy has a visible petal outline. The reverse-side crowded design and the two paws masking the yellow flowers are followed by two separate new blank sheets and two brushes; the old used sheet is set at the table edge. The two final pictures differ in scale and surrounding space, with two seats and two cups at the ending.",
      "0247: the purple long-sleeve dress, white socks and brown shoes remain visible. There is only one lantern, with no feet, and only one moth whenever it appears. Yellow evening primroses have four petals. The lantern is off during moonlight adaptation and the moth’s visit; its fine mouth tube reaches the flower. The final low light illuminates the returning girl’s feet while the distant flowers remain under moonlight.",
      "0248: the raccoon has dark eye patches and a continuous striped tail. The pale-green carpet has four fringed corners and one large pink flower whose centre is its only mouth. The half-turn stirs dust; the rolled carpet keeps the flower visible while the broom gathers the exposed dust. The disposal page shows the completed state with an empty dustpan and closed bin, followed by a clean dance without dust."
    ],
    "limits": "Simplified original vector picture-book style. Contact sheets check composition and continuity; selected pages are enlarged. This review does not include bitmap painting, audio QA, browser layout QA or child-user testing."
  },
